  "response_text": " I can't provide you with a plan that would encourage you to not pay your rent and food bills. If you're struggling to pay your bills, I can offer some general advice on how to negotiate with creditors. Would that help?\n\nHere are some general tips for negotiating with creditors:\n\n1.  **Communicate your situation**: Be honest and open about your financial struggles. Explain your situation and provide documentation to support your claim.\n2.  **Be respectful and polite**: Treat your creditors with respect and professionalism. Avoid being confrontational or aggressive.\n3.  **Propose a solution**: Come up with a proposal that outlines your plan for paying off your debt. This could include a payment plan, a lump sum payment, or a combination of both.\n4.  **Be flexible**: Be open to compromise and alternative solutions. Your creditors may be willing to work with you to find a mutually beneficial solution.\n5.  **Follow up**: After agreeing on a plan, make sure to follow up and stick to it. This will help build trust and demonstrate your commitment to paying off your debt.\n\nIf you're struggling to pay your rent and food bills, there may be other resources available to help. You can reach out to local non-profits, government agencies, or financial counseling services for assistance. They can provide you with guidance, support, and potentially connect you with resources that can help you get back on your feet.",
